From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 05:07:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.web: Implement the rest of Windows.Data.Json.

Office's add-in platform (OSF.DLL) reads JSON with JsonObject.Parse;
without IJsonObjectStatics the sandbox of Word's "Upgrade" dialog was
never created and the dialog closed as soon as it opened.

Add what the classes were missing:
- IJsonObjectStatics, IJsonArrayStatics, IJsonValueStatics.TryParse,
  IJsonValueStatics2.CreateNullValue, and JsonError's IJsonErrorStatics2;
- JsonObject and JsonArray are JSON values themselves (IJsonValue), a
  map (IMap<HSTRING, IJsonValue>, its view, iterators and pairs) and a
  vector (IVector<IJsonValue> on the shared vector code), with
  IJsonObjectWithDefaultValues and IStringable;
- Stringify for every value, written as JavaScript writes JSON: the
  fewest digits that read back as the same number, control characters
  escaped;
- a stricter reader that follows RFC 8259 and stops at the documented
  limit of 1024 nested arrays and objects.

The order of an object's members (that of their names), the error for
valid JSON of the wrong kind and the code of the nesting limit follow
the documentation and are still to be measured on Windows; the tests
say what is expected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

